        # 2
        {"kind": "h1", "text": "2. Overview & Summary"},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.1 Problem Statement"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "Email campaign work against Brevo is done by hand through a web console or by ad-hoc scripts holding a raw API key. Both are unsafe in the presence of an AI agent: a send is irreversible, outward-facing and reputation-bearing, and the Brevo API will happily accept a full-list blast as a single unguarded POST. The concrete failure this server was built after is on record — 26 of 27 Podium Tutoring campaigns were sent from a podiumtutor@gmail.com address that Brevo cannot DKIM-sign for gmail.com, which put the mail in spam and was not detected until after the fact."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.2 Proposed Solution"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": f"brevo-mcp is a Node/TypeScript MCP server, v1.0.0, that exposes {len(TOOLS)} tools ({READ_COUNT} read, {WRITE_COUNT} write) over stdio to an MCP client. Every call passes through a single HTTP client that enforces a token-bucket rate limit, retries only retryable statuses with jittered backoff, redacts the API key from every error string, and appends a JSON line to an audit log for every mutating request. Campaigns can only be created as drafts. Sending requires a literal confirm token, and every send path re-reads the campaign and checks its sender against BREVO_ENFORCE_SENDER before the request leaves the machine."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.3 Background & Context"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "The server was written for the Podium Tutoring email programme, but the only Podium-specific artefact is the default sender lock value in .env.example. It is the only server in the MCP monorepo that ships a test suite: 34 tests across src/tests/unit.test.ts and src/tests/client.test.ts, run by the Node test runner under tsx."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.4 Strategic Fit"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "It is part of the HaorGrix internal MCP tooling line, which gives agents first-class access to the operational SaaS the business already runs on. Brevo is the highest-blast-radius member of that set, so it also serves as the reference implementation for guard design — config validation at boot, confirm-string gates, audit trail, secret redaction — that the other servers are expected to adopt."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "2.5 Objectives & Business Value"},
        {"kind": "bullets", "items": [
            "Make routine campaign work (list hygiene, drafting, test sends, reporting) delegable to an agent without a human in the loop for each step.",
            "Make the one irreversible action — a full-list send — require an explicit, unambiguous human-authored token.",
            "Prevent the DKIM-misalignment class of error structurally rather than by remembering to check.",
            "Produce an accountability trail that survives the agent session, so what went out and when is answerable from disk.",
            "Report honest engagement numbers by correcting for Apple Mail Privacy Protection prefetch opens where the data allows.",
        ]},

