        # 6
        {"kind": "h1", "text": "6. Non-Functional Requirements"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Category", "Requirement"],
         "rows": [
             ["Performance", "Tool latency is dominated by the Brevo API. Local overhead is a token-bucket check and JSON serialisation. Per-request timeout is BREVO_TIMEOUT_MS (default 30s, range 1s-120s) enforced via AbortController."],
             ["Scalability", "Single process, single API key, one MCP client. Outbound throughput is capped at BREVO_RPS (default 8). getAll pages at 500 per request up to 200 pages, then refuses to continue."],
             ["Availability", "No uptime target; the process is spawned on demand by the MCP client. Resilience is per-request: retry on 408/429/5xx with jittered backoff honouring Retry-After. Brevo outages surface as BrevoApiError."],
             ["Security", "API key supplied only through the environment via dotenv, never an argument. Key format validated at boot. redact() strips any xkeysib- token from errors and audit details. Write paths gated by dry-run, sender lock and literal confirm tokens."],
             ["Privacy / Compliance", "The server handles contact email addresses and engagement events, which are personal data. It does not persist them — the audit log records method, path and status only, never request bodies. brevo_blacklist_contact provides an opt-out path. Brevo remains the system of record."],
             ["Accessibility", "N/A — no human-facing UI. Operator-facing output is plain text and JSON on stdout/stderr, readable by a screen reader through the host terminal."],
             ["Observability", "Startup banner on stderr states mode, base URL, sender lock, rps, retries and audit path. audit.jsonl is an append-only JSONL record of every mutation including attempt counts and failures. Audit write failures are reported on stderr and never fatal. No metrics endpoint and no structured read-path logging exist."],
             ["Localization", "N/A — single-locale English tool descriptions and error strings for an English-speaking operator and an English-language agent. Campaign content itself is caller-supplied and locale-agnostic."],
         ]},

