        # 8
        {"kind": "h1", "text": "8. Design & UX"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "There is no graphical interface. The product is a headless stdio process whose only consumer is an AI agent, so the design surface is the tool contract: names, descriptions, argument schemas, and the wording of results and errors."},
        {"kind": "bullets", "items": [
            "Naming: every tool is prefixed brevo_ and named verb-first against the Brevo noun (brevo_send_test_email, brevo_get_import_status), so a client listing tools from several servers never collides and the read/write intent is legible from the name alone.",
            "Descriptions as the only affordance: the agent cannot read the source, so descriptions carry the policy. brevo_create_campaign states 'Always created as a DRAFT; it is never sent by this tool' and names the follow-up tools. brevo_send_campaign_now opens with 'IRREVERSIBLE' and states the preconditions. brevo_send_test_email is labelled 'Safe'.",
            "Argument schemas as guardrails: zod bounds every numeric range (test recipients 1-10, events limit 1-1000), validates every email, and expresses confirm as a literal type so a wrong or absent token fails at schema validation before any handler runs.",
            "Confirmation ergonomics: the tokens are distinct words (SEND, SCHEDULE) rather than a shared boolean, so a confirmation cannot be copied from one call into a more dangerous one.",
            "Error legibility: refusals explain the reason and the fix in one sentence — the sender-lock error names both addresses and states that mismatch breaks DKIM alignment; DryRunError names the variable to unset; BrevoApiError carries status, Brevo's own error code and the attempt count.",
            "Result shaping: writes return a plain-language sentence naming what changed ('Campaign 42 (\"...\") is sending from ...') rather than raw API JSON, so the agent's summary to the human is accurate by default. Reads return pretty-printed JSON.",
            "Preflight as an onboarding surface: brevo_preflight returns a pass/fail/warn checklist rather than raw payloads, giving the agent a single call that establishes whether work can proceed.",
        ]},

        # 9
